Availability Domain: Isolated from each other, fault toleance, unlikily to fail simultaniuosly. 
 - Each availability Domain has three FD
 - Logical data center within an AD

FD: A fault domain is a subdivision of an AD. Each availability domain contains three fault domains. Fault domains let you distribute your instances so that they are not on the same physical hardware within a single availability domain. A fault domain cannot be associated with multiple availability domains.


